msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:99
#: 07e5b5d9e1804c83a1344807f9d02237
msgid "SERIAL3 = GPS1 = USART6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:100
#: 76f38a6c83424fee83c5dd952ca84f2e
msgid "SERIAL4 = GPS2 = UART4 (if :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` = 2 or 3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:101
#: 0362d06b8aaf4d908c4a0cf1938f5eb9
msgid "SERIAL5 = not assigned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:102
#: 8460f02ea32d4d1c9c8e47920103dd1b
msgid "SERIAL6 = not assigned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:104
#: 81d2f36d753847f7bdab84e3a021f9bc
msgid "Serial protocols can be adjusted to personal preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:107
#: a15f1360fbfb4895a03f9b918bb6d492
msgid "Dshot capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:109
#: 22ac25e511d44d3785e64d3c14b59224
msgid "All motor/servo outputs are Dshot and PWM capable. However, mixing Dshot and normal PWM operation for outputs is restricted into groups, ie. enabling Dshot for an output in a group requires that ALL outputs in that group be configured and used as Dshot, rather than PWM outputs. The output groups that must be the same (PWM rate or Dshot, when configured as a normal servo/motor output) are: 1/2/6, 3/4/5, 7/8(Pro only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:112
#: 1ff38a23c9e34126a9626119b75e08ca
msgid "Flashing Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:113
#: 9f29d4abee8d49f387fa78603c0507ff
msgid "Usually these boards are sold pre-flashed with betaflight / INav firwares and require both firmware and bootloader to be updated if you want to use ArduPilot, as an ArduPilot-compatible bootloader is required for subsequent ArduPilot firmware-upgrade handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:115
#: 6f824c8bfa5b4fc6bce6d144f3200fea
msgid "Firmware files can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/>`__. Use omnibusf4pro firmware for the OmnibusF4Pro boards and omnibusf4 firmware for the AIO versions. The pro version will be used in the following examples. Besides the .apj files for firmware flashing via MissionPlanner, there's also .hex files for use with various utilities like dfu-util or betaflight / iNav GUIs. You will also find a _bl.hex that contains the firmware plus the ArduPilot compatible bootloader in case it is not already present on your board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:119
#: 993d1c1d9983471988624a11948505b2
msgid "The provided _bl.hex file can be flashed using BF or iNav GUI, likely the most convenient way to get ArduPilot on your board the first time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-omnibusf4pro.rst:121
#: 03e2518b497f4d538cf5d3729757c733
msgid "Alternatively, the bootloader can be flashed separately. This requires the board to be put into DFU mode. Tools like dfu-util can be used to flash the bootlader. Once the bootlader is present, all subsequent firmware updates can be done using MissionPlanner's firmware functions."
msgstr ""

